.\" objcli(1) man page
.TH OBJCLI 1 "2026-05-29" "objcli" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
objcli \- unified CLI for AWS S3 and Tencent Cloud COS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B objcli
.RI < cp | mv | sync | rm | ls | presign | resume | version >
.RI [ args... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B objcli
is a unified CLI for object storage that wraps AWS S3 and Tencent Cloud COS.
It supports cloud-to-cloud and local-to-cloud copy, move, sync, remove, list,
and presign operations. Paths use a URL-style notation:
.IP \(bu 2
.B cos://<bucket>.<region>/<key-or-prefix>
.IP \(bu 2
.B s3://<bucket>.<region>/<key-or-prefix>
.IP \(bu 2
local filesystem path (for cp / sync only)
.PP
A URL is treated as a prefix when it contains
.BR * ,
ends with
.BR / ,
or has an empty key.

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B cp <SRC> <DST>
Copy objects. Supports cloud<->cloud and local<->cloud directions.
Automatically chooses PutObject or Multipart upload based on size.
.TP
.B mv <SRC> <DST>
Move objects (= cp followed by removal of source).
.TP
.B sync <SRC> <DST>
Incremental sync between two locations. Supports
.B --delete
and
.BR --size-only .
.TP
.B rm <TARGET>
Remove a single object, a prefix, or a list of URLs.
.TP
.B ls <TARGET>
List objects. Exit codes follow Linux
.BR ls (1):
non-zero when the target does not exist.
.TP
.B presign <TARGET>
Generate a presigned URL (GET or PUT).
.TP
.B resume
Manage multipart upload resume state. Subcommands:
.B list
and
.BR abort .
.TP
.B version
Print version, commit hash, build time, and Go version.

.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -o " text|json"
Output format. Defaults to text.
.TP
.BR -exclude " PATTERN"
Glob pattern for files/keys to exclude. May be specified multiple times.
.TP
.BR -include " PATTERN"
Glob pattern to re-include previously excluded items. May be specified
multiple times. Order matters and matches AWS CLI semantics.
.TP
.BR -bandwidth " RATE"
Limit transfer rate, e.g.
.BR 10MB/s ,
.BR 100KiB/s ,
.BR 1Gbps .
0 disables limiting.
.TP
.BR -retries " N"
Retry attempts on transient errors. Defaults to 3.
.TP
.BR -retry-base-ms " MS"
Base interval (milliseconds) for exponential backoff between retries.
Defaults to 200.

.SH CREDENTIALS
.TP
.B S3
.B -s3-ak
/
.B -s3-sk
on the command line, or
.B AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID
/
.B AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY
in the environment.
.TP
.B COS
.B -cos-id
/
.B -cos-sk
on the command line, or
.B TENCENT_SECRET_ID
/
.B TENCENT_SECRET_KEY
(or the legacy
.B COS_SECRET_ID
/
.B COS_SECRET_KEY )
in the environment.
.TP
.B S3-compatible
.B -s3-endpoint
to point at a non-AWS endpoint such as MinIO.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Operation finished with errors (partial or total failure).
.TP
.B 2
Argument error, or
.BR ls (1)-style
"target does not exist".

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID ", " AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY
S3 credentials.
.TP
.BR TENCENT_SECRET_ID ", " TENCENT_SECRET_KEY
COS credentials.
.TP
.BR COS_SECRET_ID ", " COS_SECRET_KEY
COS credentials (alternative names).
.TP
.BR TASKOBS_BUCKET ", " TASKOBS_REGION ", " TASKOBS_SECRET_ID ", " TASKOBS_SECRET_KEY ", " TASKOBS_BASE_URL ", " TASKOBS_TASK
taskobserver runtime monitoring config.

.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Copy a single object from S3 to COS:
.nf
.B "objcli cp s3://srcb.us-east-1/data.zip cos://dstb.ap-beijing/data.zip"
.fi
.PP
Recursive prefix copy:
.nf
.B "objcli cp cos://b1.ap-beijing/logs/ cos://b2.ap-shanghai/backup/ -r"
.fi
.PP
Glob remove with force:
.nf
.B "objcli rm 'cos://b.ap-beijing/tmp/*' -r -f"
.fi
.PP
Incremental sync from local to COS, delete extras at destination:
.nf
.B "objcli sync /local/dir/ cos://b.ap-beijing/dir/ --delete"
.fi
.PP
Issue a presigned GET URL valid for one hour:
.nf
.B "objcli presign cos://b.ap-beijing/file.zip -expires 3600"
.fi
.PP
Throttle a large copy to 50 MB/s with 5 retries:
.nf
.B "objcli cp s3://b.ap-east-1/big.tar cos://b.ap-beijing/big.tar -bandwidth 50MB/s -retries 5"
.fi

.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.objcli/resume/
Multipart upload resume state files.

